================================================================================
THIRD-PARTY CODE
================================================================================

This repository vendors and ports published baseline models. Each retains its
original authors' license, kept alongside the vendored source. The MIT terms
above apply to this project's own code, NOT to these components.

1. ATCNet — Altaheri et al. 2023
   Upstream: https://github.com/Altaheri/EEG-ATCNet  (Apache License 2.0)
   Vendored: code/models/atcnet/_official_keras/  (incl. its LICENSE)
   Port:     code/models/atcnet/atcnet_torch.py   (Keras -> PyTorch, 1:1)
   Derived:  code/models/atcnet/atcnet_s4.py      (reuses the conv block)

2. EEGNet — Lawhern et al. 2018
   Upstream: https://github.com/vlawhern/arl-eegmodels
   Vendored: code/models/paper_baselines/_official/EEGModels_arl_keras.py
             + LICENSE_arl-eegmodels.txt
   Port:     code/models/paper_baselines/eegnet_official_torch.py

3. EEGNeX — Chen et al. 2024
   Upstream: https://github.com/chenxiachan/EEGNeX
   Vendored: code/models/paper_baselines/_official/BenchmarkModels_eegnex_keras.py
             + LICENSE_EEGNeX.md
   Port:     code/models/paper_baselines/eegnex_official_torch.py

4. EEG-Deformer — Ding et al. 2024
   Upstream: https://github.com/yi-ding-cs/EEG-Deformer
   Vendored: code/models/paper_baselines/_official/EEGDeformer.py
   Run unmodified (no port).

5. S4 / DINO-DualCD family
   Adapted from an advisor-supplied package whose own lineage is the ERP-Benchmark
   codebase (arXiv:2601.00573). Deviations are recorded in
   code/models/eeg_foundation/README.md. Note that the state-space layer is a
   DIAGONAL SSM, not the DPLR construction of Gu et al. (ICLR 2022) — see
   docs/PLAN_cross_subject_benchmark_and_fusion.md §5.5.

================================================================================
DATA
================================================================================

No EEG data is distributed with this repository. Both datasets are third-party
and must be obtained from their sources under their own terms:

* WBCIC-SHU (2C and 3C) — Yang et al., Scientific Data 12:488 (2025),
  doi:10.1038/s41597-025-04826-y; data at doi:10.25452/figshare.plus.22671172
  (CC-BY-4.0).
* SHU 2022 — Ma et al.; per-session .mat files as released by the authors.

Paths to local copies live in gitignored `code/configs/paths.local.yaml`.
